Aether OS Licensing Notice
==========================

Aether OS is a multi-license project.  No single license covers every file or
every generated release artifact.

Aether Core
-----------

The project-authored kernel, boot, driver, filesystem, network, cryptography,
and kernel-support sources identified in LICENSING.md are licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version
(SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later).

The complete license text is in:

    LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt

Outer project components
------------------------

The project-authored user applications, public userspace ABI, shared parser
library, build and development tools, tests, documentation, examples, and
other outer components identified in LICENSING.md are licensed under the MIT
License (SPDX: MIT).

The complete license text is in:

    LICENSES/MIT.txt

Third-party material
--------------------

Vendored, adapted, generated, and externally sourced material retains its
upstream license.  See THIRD_PARTY.md and notices stored with those components.
Neither GPL-3.0-or-later nor MIT relicenses third-party material.

The authoritative path-by-path boundary and binary-distribution rules are in
LICENSING.md.

Historical MIT grants
---------------------

Versions of Aether code already received under the MIT License remain usable
under that grant.  Open-source licenses already granted for those copies are
not withdrawn.  The GPL-3.0-or-later boundary governs the core in repository
versions that carry this notice and new core contributions made under it.
